# Docker build context exclusions. The context is `engine/` (compose.yaml
# `build.context: ..`), so `deploy/.env` — which holds the live
# TEMPO_ENGINE_TOKEN and HF_TOKEN — is inside it and would otherwise be
# handed to the Docker daemon on every `docker compose up --build`.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs exactly two things: `pyproject.toml` and
# `tempo_engine/`. Nothing here may exclude either, and nothing in the image
# needs an env file — `.env.example` is repository documentation, read by
# humans and by brev-deploy.sh, never by the build.
#
# Regression-pinned by engine/tests/test_app_contract.py::
# test_docker_build_context_excludes_secrets.

# Secrets: every .env, at any depth, including the example.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Model weights and index artifacts, if anyone ever points the context at them.
models/
*.pkl
*.npz

# Python and tool caches.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Local noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/